{
  "$comment": [
    "The tournament ranking rule as executable cases. Read by BOTH suites - the Node tests in",
    "src/domain/tournament/ranking.test.ts and the JUnit tests in RankingEngineVectorTest - so the",
    "TypeScript and Java implementations cannot drift apart without a test failing.",
    "",
    "The dimensions are WinPoint -> Diff -> Head-to-head -> Average Score. Head-to-head is sparse,",
    "so Average Score builds a complete BASELINE ordering first and head-to-head is then applied as",
    "a corrective pass inside each group tied on WinPoint AND Diff. That is implementation order,",
    "not priority: inside such a group an available head-to-head result overrides Average Score,",
    "and Average Score decides a pair only where head-to-head says nothing. Equal averages are NOT",
    "an exemption. Average Score = scoreFor / games; a no-opponent game counts on both sides of",
    "that division, a penalty on neither.",
    "",
    "A meeting with winner:null is a draw. A meeting with penalty:true is not a game and must be",
    "ignored entirely. 'aggregations' is the number of FULL head-to-head aggregations the engine is",
    "allowed to perform - it pins the laziness requirement, not just the ordering."
  ],
